  "id": "COMPOUND:16938 - PROTEIN:585",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 3-Epi-29-Acetoxystelliferin E may act as a target for Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is linked to G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, which is a target of (12S)-15-methoxy-11-methyl-3,5-dioxa-11-azapentacyclo[10.7.1.02,6.08,20.014,19]icosa-1(20),2(6),7,14(19),15,17-hexaene, a compound that ultimately targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. Similarly, the drug is also linked to Forkhead box protein O1, which is a target of Beta-Amyrone, which in turn targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. Additionally, the drug is connected to G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, which is a target of Rubramin, another compound that also targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. These pathways suggest a potential mechanism where 3-Epi-29-Acetoxystelliferin E may influence Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through the regulation of cyclin-D1 and other downstream targets. The evidence supports a network of interactions where the drug may modulate the activity of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase via indirect pathways involving cyclin-D1 and other proteins.",
